I encountered something that may or may not represent a bug in the
routines for eating and deciding if a corpse is rotted.

My character was down real low on strength, so when I killed a giant,
its corpse was too good to pass up.  Even though I was satiated at the
time.  I .'ed enough moves to be reasonably sure I wouldn't die taking
the first bite.  Then, still satiated, I chowed down.

After each "stop eating?" message I waited another 20 turns, then
started again.  There must have been 20 or so of these messages -- for a
total of about 450 moves between the time the giant became a corpse, and
the corpse was completely eaten (counting the time I waited at the
beginning, and some miscellaneous fighting).  Yet the meat never got
tainted, or even just rotten.

I've used the same technique to eat dragon corpses.  Is it really a bug,
or do big corpses just stay fresh for many hundreds of moves?

